WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:08.816
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.116 --> 00:00:14.114
Unit eighteen: Editing and Proofreading. Today you will check and improve your own writing.

4
00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.741
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.805
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:22.419
Edit.

7
00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:26.264
Edit means to improve a text by changing it.

8
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.304
Edit your first draft.

9
00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:31.116
Your turn. Say: Edit.

10
00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:34.712
Edit.

11
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:36.416
Proofread.

12
00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:40.043
Proofread means to check for small mistakes.

13
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.290
Always proofread your work.

14
00:00:42.883 --> 00:00:45.756
Your turn. Say: Proofread.

15
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.601
Proofread.

16
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.165
Draft.

17
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.765
Draft means an early version of a text.

18
00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.897
This is my first draft.

19
00:00:57.483 --> 00:00:59.764
Your turn. Say: Draft.

20
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.369
Draft.

21
00:01:04.117 --> 00:01:05.083
Spelling.

22
00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:08.187
Spelling means how words are written.

23
00:01:08.783 --> 00:01:10.028
Check your spelling.

24
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:12.979
Your turn. Say: Spelling.

25
00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:16.858
Spelling.

26
00:01:17.617 --> 00:01:18.420
Grammar.

27
00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:21.579
Grammar means the rules of a language.

28
00:01:22.183 --> 00:01:23.359
Check the grammar.

29
00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.800
Your turn. Say: Grammar.

30
00:01:29.633 --> 00:01:30.623
Grammar.

31
00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:32.350
Revise.

32
00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:36.104
Revise means to change something to make it better.

33
00:01:36.717 --> 00:01:38.739
Revise the second paragraph.

34
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.548
Your turn. Say: Revise.

35
00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.459
Revise.

36
00:01:47.217 --> 00:01:48.020
Feedback.

37
00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:51.457
Feedback means advice about how to improve.

38
00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.504
Ask for feedback.

39
00:01:54.117 --> 00:01:56.641
Your turn. Say: Feedback.

40
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:00.443
Feedback.

41
00:02:01.183 --> 00:02:02.277
Consistent.

42
00:02:03.283 --> 00:02:05.724
Consistent means always the same in style.

43
00:02:06.317 --> 00:02:08.223
Keep your tenses consistent.

44
00:02:08.817 --> 00:02:11.202
Your turn. Say: Consistent.

45
00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.161
Consistent.

46
00:02:15.967 --> 00:02:19.327
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.183 --> 00:02:22.345
Visal, how can I improve my writing?

48
00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:34.000
Write a first draft without stopping. Then revise it: check the ideas and the order. After that, edit the language and proofread.

49
00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:37.118
What should I check when I proofread?

50
00:02:38.217 --> 00:02:46.709
Check spelling, punctuation, capital letters and grammar such as verb forms. Read it aloud to find mistakes.

51
00:02:47.817 --> 00:02:49.166
What about feedback?

52
00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:55.712
Ask a friend or teacher to read it. Fresh eyes find mistakes you cannot see yourself.

53
00:02:56.867 --> 00:02:58.611
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.448
Grammar focus: Checklist with have to.

55
00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:03.900
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.407
You have to check the spelling.

57
00:03:07.317 --> 00:03:09.003
She has to revise the draft.

58
00:03:09.967 --> 00:03:14.895
Use have to or has to for a strong duty. After have to, use the base verb.

59
00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:19.196
Be careful! Don't say: You have to checking spelling.

60
00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.412
Say: You have to check spelling.

61
00:03:23.712 --> 00:03:25.061
Use base verb.

62
00:03:25.867 --> 00:03:28.658
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:30.781
Checking My Essay.

64
00:03:31.081 --> 00:03:34.021
Srey Mom finishes her first draft on Monday.

65
00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:38.159
On Tuesday she revises the ideas and the order.

66
00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:41.932
Then she edits the grammar and checks the spelling.

67
00:03:42.933 --> 00:03:45.897
She reads the essay aloud to find small mistakes.

68
00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.608
Finally, her teacher gives her useful feedback.

69
00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:54.922
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:55.783 --> 00:03:57.678
A draft is an early blank.

71
00:03:57.978 --> 00:04:01.237
A, version. B, meal. C, coin.

72
00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.335
The answer is A: version.

73
00:04:07.483 --> 00:04:09.645
Proofread means to check small blank.

74
00:04:09.945 --> 00:04:13.518
A, doors. B, mistakes. C, prices.

75
00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:19.310
The answer is B: mistakes.

76
00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.275
Feedback is advice to blank.

77
00:04:22.575 --> 00:04:25.962
A, forget. B, pay. C, improve.

78
00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.558
The answer is C: improve.

79
00:04:32.717 --> 00:04:34.647
Revise means to make it blank.

80
00:04:34.947 --> 00:04:37.892
A, better. B, wet. C, far.

81
00:04:41.433 --> 00:04:43.328
The answer is A: better.

82
00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:46.483
Srey Mom reads the essay blank.

83
00:04:46.783 --> 00:04:50.158
A, upside. B, aloud. C, never.

84
00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.444
The answer is B: aloud.

85
00:04:56.633 --> 00:04:59.971
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:00.817 --> 00:05:02.491
How do you proofread your writing?

87
00:05:11.283 --> 00:05:12.842
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:13.142 --> 00:05:25.224
I write a first draft, then revise the ideas and edit the language. I check spelling, punctuation and grammar, and I read the text aloud. I also ask for feedback.

89
00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:27.315
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:28.217 --> 00:05:32.158
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and checklist with have to.

91
00:05:32.458 --> 00:05:37.548
Today's value is meticulousness. Check every detail carefully before you trust it.

92
00:05:37.848 --> 00:05:40.466
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:40.766 --> 00:05:43.348
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

